        <history>
          <p>Written alongside ‘Greeting’ in the mid-1890s, ‘Summer Song’ sets another Holstein text celebrating the Danish summer landscape. The two songs were conceived as a pair and were premiered together, and they are often still performed as companion pieces in recital, sharing key, tempo character, and poetic subject.</p>
